@@ -74,6 +74,32 @@ enable_token_export = true
 
 Leave it unset for normal training. When enabled, it exports every sequence from each exporting rank.
 
+## Exact snapshot rollout budgets
+
+Experiments that require every optimizer batch to use exactly one policy
+snapshot can enable the orchestrator's low-throughput strict mode:
+
+```toml
+[orchestrator]
+max_off_policy_steps = 0
+strict_snapshot_batches = true
+train_groups_per_policy = 1
+
+[weight_broadcast]
+type = "filesystem"
+```
+
+`train_groups_per_policy` counts complete source environment groups admitted
+for one policy version; it does not count optimizer batches or serialized
+traces. One source group can expand into enough traces for a full optimizer
+batch, so use `1` whenever a single group fills the batch. Strict mode stops
+opening groups after that number, waits until the trainer's filesystem
+checkpoint has been fully applied to inference, runs any evaluation scheduled
+for that snapshot to completion, and only then opens the next training cohort.
+Use it for exact call accounting and snapshot-aligned evaluation, not
+throughput-oriented production runs. The config validator rejects nonzero
+`max_off_policy_steps` and non-filesystem weight broadcast in this mode.
+
 ## Key files
 
 - `packages/prime-rl-configs/src/prime_rl/` — config classes under `configs/`; `utils/config.py` re-exports `BaseConfig` and `cli`
